Asha is ready to leave.
Before leaving, she explains the rules about Moti.
She says, "Maya, this is his feeding schedule."
"Feed him at exactly eight o'clock in the morning."
"And feed him at exactly eight o'clock at night too."
"Food must be given exactly on time."
I listen to everything carefully.
She says again, "In the park, keep him on the leash."
"Letting him loose in the park must not be done."
"He must not wander far."
Asha is very serious.
She says, "Human food must strictly not be given to him."
"Our snacks must never be given to him."
"This is very important."
I smile.
I say, "Asha, do not worry."
"I understand all your rules."
"I will look after him well."
Asha is satisfied.
She thanks me.
